# ***************************************************
# * Repo root. crm/ and whatbot/ have their own too.
# ***************************************************
# A sub-.gitignore only covers its own folder, so anything at the root or
# in docs/ is unprotected without this file. That includes real payroll
# sheets and Diane transcripts.

# ===============================
# * Secrets
# ===============================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ===============================
# * Real business data. Never commit.
# ===============================
# Payroll sheets, wherever they land. The live one is docs/master.xlsx.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv

# Diane's exported conversations and the boss's own files.
docs/boss/
docs/downloads/

# Server build notes: hardware, addresses, access.
lithu server.txt
server setup.png

# ===============================
# * Generated and local
# ===============================
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
crm/api/public/assets/
crm/api/generated/

# Verification scripts: written to check one thing, then deleted. Committing
# one leaves dead code holding real credentials.
_*.js

# A generated Diane scenario. It is different every run by design, so a
# committed one is somebody reading last week's conversation.
crm/api/scripts/.review.txt
crm/api/scripts/.closure.txt
crm/api/scripts/.audit.txt

npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
